  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening organizational processes to reduce vulnerability in Central America region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD will oversee the management of the regional Sustainable Livelihood with DRR approach programme in Central America 2009-2013 (covering four countries: Nicaragua, Honduras, El Salvador, Guatemala) and play a coordination and facilitation role in its delivery &#x2013; in particular with regards the activities of the regional partner network related to learning and experience sharing between partners and more widely.  It This programme is supported by two important funds, the &#x201C;Haramead Trust and a Major Donor&#x201D; for the next three years. An important part will be to introduce and work with partners on the application of monitoring tools to effectively measure improvements in quality of life and to help partners plan a more comprehensive DRR approach at an institutional level. This internal project is essential to achieving the overall programme aim of contributing to improve the livelihoods of 21,802 beneficiaries, through the implementation of sustainable agricultural practices and the incidence in public policy to ensure access, control and management of natural resources by the communities.

This internal grant includes funding for the hosting and organisation of annual events / workshops, establishment and administration of a virtual learning platform, partner exchange visits, promotion of increased co-ordination and learning between the regional partner network and other networks and regional programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
